RObject -- R object
*******************

  * Usage: 
        RObject x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, a Macaulay2 object; 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note R object: RObject,, the R equivalent of x; 

Description
===========

An RObject is a SEXP (pointer) to an R object in memory.  Note that in R, most
objects are actually vectors, and scalars are just vectors of length 1.

RObject is a *note SelfInitializingType: (Macaulay2Doc)SelfInitializingType,,
and so it acts as its own constructor method.  When passed a Macaulay2 object
as input, the corresponding R object is returned.  See the converting to R
objects section below for the supported input types.

Each RObject is displayed by calling R's capture.output function.

+----------------------------+
|i1 : RObject {2, 4, 6, 8}   |
|                            |
|o1 = [1] 2 4 6 8            |
|                            |
|o1 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+
|i2 : RObject pi             |
|                            |
|o2 = [1] 3.141593           |
|                            |
|o2 : RObject of type double |
+----------------------------+

It is converted to a string using R's toString function.

+----------------------------------+
|i3 : toString RObject {2, 4, 6, 8}|
|                                  |
|o3 = 2, 4, 6, 8                   |
+----------------------------------+
