new RObject from Boolean -- create an R logical vector from a Boolean
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        RObject x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note R object: RObject,, a logical vector of length 1; 

Description
===========

Converts a Macaulay2 *note Boolean: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean, to an R logical
vector of length 1.

+----------------------------+
|i1 : RObject true           |
|                            |
|o1 = [1] TRUE               |
|                            |
|o1 : RObject of type logical|
+----------------------------+
|i2 : RObject false          |
|                            |
|o2 = [1] FALSE              |
|                            |
|o2 : RObject of type logical|
+----------------------------+

Another logical vector without a Macaulay2 equivalent is *note NA: NA,.

See also
========

  * *note NA: NA, -- missing value
  * *note new RObject from List: new RObject from List, -- create an R vector
    from a list
  * *note not RObject: not RObject, -- logical negation of an R object
  * *note RObject and RObject: RObject and RObject, -- logical conjunction of R
    objects

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note new RObject from Boolean: new RObject from Boolean, -- create an R
    logical vector from a Boolean
