new RObject from HashTable -- create an R environment from a hash table
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        RObject t
  * Inputs:
      * t, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, with *note String:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String, keys;
  * Outputs:
      * a *note R object: RObject,, an R environment; 

Description
===========

Converts a Macaulay2 *note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, with *note
String: (Macaulay2Doc)String, keys to an R environment, with each key-value
pair becoming a variable binding.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : env = RObject hashTable {"x" => 5_ZZ, "y" => 2_ZZ}|
|                                                       |
|o1 = <environment: 0x7f118e75cf60>                     |
|                                                       |
|o1 : RObject of type environment                       |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : RValue("x^y", Environment => env)                 |
|                                                       |
|o2 = [1] 25                                            |
|                                                       |
|o2 : RObject of type double                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : value oo                                          |
|                                                       |
|o3 = 25                                                |
|                                                       |
|o3 : RR (of precision 53)                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note new RObject from HashTable: new RObject from HashTable, -- create an
    R environment from a hash table
