new RObject from Matrix -- create an R matrix from a Macaulay2 matrix
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        RObject A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note R object: RObject,, an R matrix; 

Description
===========

Converts a Macaulay2 *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, to an R matrix.  Since
Macaulay2 uses row-major order and R uses column-major order, the matrix is
transposed during conversion so that the displayed values match.

+----------------------------+
|i1 : A = random(ZZ^2, ZZ^3) |
|                            |
|o1 = | 8 3 8 |              |
|     | 1 7 3 |              |
|                            |
|              2       3     |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ      |
+----------------------------+
|i2 : RObject A              |
|                            |
|o2 =      [,1] [,2] [,3]    |
|     [1,]    8    3    8    |
|     [2,]    1    7    3    |
|                            |
|o2 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+

Note that *note value(RObject): value_lpRObject_rp, does not undo this
transposition, so value and RObject are not exact inverses when applied to
matrices.

+-----------------------------+
|i3 : value oo                |
|                             |
|o3 = {{8, 1}, {3, 7}, {8, 3}}|
|                             |
|o3 : List                    |
+-----------------------------+
|i4 : A == transpose matrix oo|
|                             |
|o4 = true                    |
+-----------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note value(RObject): value_lpRObject_rp, -- convert R object to Macaulay2

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note new RObject from Matrix: new RObject from Matrix, -- create an R
    matrix from a Macaulay2 matrix
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

