**********************************

  * Operator: *note +: (Macaulay2Doc)+,
  * Usage: 
        x + y
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note R object: RObject,, 
      * y, a *note R object: RObject,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note R object: RObject,, the sum of x and y; 

Description
===========

Add two R objects.

+----------------------------+
|i1 : x = RObject 5          |
|                            |
|o1 = [1] 5                  |
|                            |
|o1 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+
|i2 : y = RObject 2          |
|                            |
|o2 = [1] 2                  |
|                            |
|o2 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+
|i3 : x + y                  |
|                            |
|o3 = [1] 7                  |
|                            |
|o3 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+

It may also be used as a unary operator.

+----------------------------+
|i4 : +x                     |
|                            |
|o4 = [1] 5                  |
|                            |
|o4 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+

One of the operands may be a Macaulay2 object.  It will be converted to an
*note RObject: RObject, before the operation is performed.

+----------------------------+
|i5 : x + 2                  |
|                            |
|o5 = [1] 7                  |
|                            |
|o5 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+
|i6 : 5 + y                  |
|                            |
|o6 = [1] 7                  |
|                            |
|o6 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+

