RObject : RObject -- R colon operator
*************************************

  * Operator: *note _colon_: (Macaulay2Doc)_co,
  * Usage: 
        x : y
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note R object: RObject,, 
      * y, a *note R object: RObject,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note R object: RObject,, the sequence of integers from x to y; 

Description
===========

Generate the sequence between two numbers with step size 1 (or -1 if the first
number is greater than the second).  This operator is available both as :, as
in R, or .., its Macaulay2 equivalent.

+----------------------------+
|i1 : x = RObject 2          |
|                            |
|o1 = [1] 2                  |
|                            |
|o1 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+
|i2 : y = RObject 7          |
|                            |
|o2 = [1] 7                  |
|                            |
|o2 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+
|i3 : x:y                    |
|                            |
|o3 = [1] 2 3 4 5 6 7        |
|                            |
|o3 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+
|i4 : y:x                    |
|                            |
|o4 = [1] 7 6 5 4 3 2        |
|                            |
|o4 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+
|i5 : x..y                   |
|                            |
|o5 = [1] 2 3 4 5 6 7        |
|                            |
|o5 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+

One of the operands may be a Macaulay2 object.  It will be converted to an
*note RObject: RObject, before the operation is performed. An exception is that
when using the : operator and the first argument given is a Macaulay2 *note ZZ:
(Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, object, *note ZZ _colon_ Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ _co Thing,
will be called instead.

+----------------------------+
|i6 : x:7                    |
|                            |
|o6 = [1] 2 3 4 5 6 7        |
|                            |
|o6 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+
|i7 : 2:y                    |
|                            |
|o7 = ([1] 7, [1] 7)         |
|                            |
|o7 : Sequence               |
+----------------------------+
|i8 : 2..y                   |
|                            |
|o8 = [1] 2 3 4 5 6 7        |
|                            |
|o8 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note RObject + RObject: RObject + RObject, -- add R objects

