~ RObject -- bitwise NOT of an R object, or create a one-sided formula
**********************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ~: (Macaulay2Doc)~,
  * Usage: 
        ~x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note R object: RObject,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note R object: RObject,, the bitwise NOT of x (integer or real
        input),; or a one-sided R formula ~x (all other inputs)

Description
===========

For integer and real R vectors, *note ~: (Macaulay2Doc)~, computes bitwise NOT,
calling R's bitwNot.

+----------------------------+
|i1 : x = RObject 12         |
|                            |
|o1 = [1] 12                 |
|                            |
|o1 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+
|i2 : ~x                     |
|                            |
|o2 = [1] -13                |
|                            |
|o2 : RObject of type integer|
+----------------------------+

For all other types, *note ~: (Macaulay2Doc)~, creates a one-sided R formula,
equivalent to R's ~x.  This is the same operator used for two-sided formulas;
see *note RObject ~ RObject: RObject ~ RObject,.

+-----------------------------+
|i3 : ~ RQuote "x"            |
|                             |
|o3 = .Primitive("~")(x)      |
|                             |
|o3 : RObject of type language|
+-----------------------------+

