RFunction -- R function
***********************

  * Usage: 
        RFunction x
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, or a *note thing:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, specifying an R function;
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note RFunction: RFunction,, 

Description
===========

An RFunction is a function that wraps around an R function specified by a
string.  Its arguments are converted to *note RObject: RObject,'s.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : qnorm = RFunction "qnorm"          |
|                                        |
|o1 = qnorm                              |
|                                        |
|o1 : RFunction                          |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : qnorm(0.025, "lower.tail" => false)|
|                                        |
|o2 = [1] 1.959964                       |
|                                        |
|o2 : RObject of type double             |
+----------------------------------------+

Any Macaulay2 object may also be used; it is converted to a string with *note
toString: (Macaulay2Doc)toString,.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : RFunction sin                                                          |
|                                                                            |
|o3 = RFunction[../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/RInterface.m2:145:4-150:15]|
|                                                                            |
|o3 : RFunction                                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : oo(pi/4)                                                               |
|                                                                            |
|o4 = [1] 0.7071068                                                          |
|                                                                            |
|o4 : RObject of type double                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
* Menu:

* library::                     load an R package

Methods that use an object of class RFunction:
==============================================

  * "new RFunction from RObject"
  * "new RFunction from String"
  * "new RFunction from Thing"

