RContext -- R context
*********************

Description
===========

An RContext is a wrapper around an R environment that keeps track of variable
bindings across a series of R computations.

Create an empty context with new RContext:

+-----------------------+
|i1 : ctx = new RContext|
|                       |
|o1 = ctx               |
|                       |
|o1 : RContext          |
+-----------------------+

Alternatively, pass an R code string to initialize the context with variable
bindings.  See *note new RContext from String: new RContext from String,.

See also
========

  * *note RValue: RValue, -- evaluate R code
* Menu:

* new RContext from String::    construct an R context
* RContext String::             evaluate R code in a context
* RContext _ String: RContext _us String.  get a variable from an R context
* listSymbols(RContext): listSymbols_lpRObject_rp.  list symbols in an R environment
* use(RContext): use_lpRContext_rp.  import R context variables into Macaulay2

Methods that use a R context:
=============================

  * "listSymbols(RContext)" -- see *note listSymbols(RObject):
    listSymbols_lpRObject_rp, -- list symbols in an R environment
  * *note new RContext from String: new RContext from String, -- construct an R
    context
  * "new RContext"
  * *note RContext _ String: RContext _us String, -- get a variable from an R
    context
  * *note RContext String: RContext String, -- evaluate R code in a context
  * *note use(RContext): use_lpRContext_rp, -- import R context variables into
    Macaulay2

For the programmer
==================

The object *note RContext: RContext, is a *note self initializing type:
(Macaulay2Doc)SelfInitializingType,, with ancestor classes *note
MutableHashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)MutableHashTable, < *note HashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, < *note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

