RQuote -- create an unevaluated R symbol
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        RQuote str
  * Inputs:
      * str, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String, or a *note thing:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note R object: RObject,, an R symbol (type symbol); 

Description
===========

Create an unevaluated R symbol.  This is analogous to R's quote function, and
is useful when a symbol itself (rather than its value) needs to be passed to an
R function.

Compare the behavior of *note RSymbol: RSymbol,, which evaluates the symbol and
returns its value:

+---------------------------+
|i1 : RSymbol "pi"          |
|                           |
|o1 = [1] 3.141593          |
|                           |
|o1 : RObject of type double|
+---------------------------+
|i2 : RQuote "pi"           |
|                           |
|o2 = pi                    |
|                           |
|o2 : RObject of type symbol|
+---------------------------+

A Macaulay2 *note Symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol, may also be used.

+---------------------------+
|i3 : RQuote pi             |
|                           |
|o3 = pi                    |
|                           |
|o3 : RObject of type symbol|
+---------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note RSymbol: RSymbol, -- look up an R object by name

Ways to use RQuote:
===================

  * "RQuote(String)"
  * "RQuote(Thing)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note RQuote: RQuote, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

